                        # So for the move to be valid, we need that no neighbor of vtx is colored c_low
                        # in the current state? Not exactly: because if a neighbor is c_low and in the
                        # Kempe component, it will become target_color, so no conflict.
                        # The condition is that the Kempe component does not contain any vertex
                        # that is colored c_low and adjacent to vtx? Actually, after swap, vtx becomes c_low.
                        # So we need that no neighbor of vtx is colored c_low after the swap.
                        # After swap, a neighbor u of vtx:
                        #   - if u was target_color and in component -> becomes c_low -> conflict if u adjacent to vtx? 
                        #     but u is neighbor of vtx, so if u becomes c_low and vtx becomes c_low -> conflict.
                        #   - if u was c_low and in component -> becomes target_color -> no conflict.
                        #   - if u was target_color and not in component -> remains target_color -> no conflict.
                        #   - if u was c_low and not in component -> remains c_low -> conflict.
                        # Therefore, to avoid conflict, we must ensure that no neighbor of vtx that is
                        # colored c_low is outside the Kempe component.
